// The coherence order that admitted an execution is assertable as `.co`.
//
// MoRDor's own test, for #66. Thread 1 writes x twice, so any execution
// containing both writes has a non-empty coherence order between them, and
// program order forces 2 before 3. Before this the order was searched for,
// used and thrown away with the search, so no assertion could name it and
// "why was this execution admitted?" had no answer from the tool.
//
// (2,3) is the pair of writes in the order the search settles on; the reverse
// is excluded by po, which try_all_coherence_orders filters permutations by.
x := 0;
{
  x := 1;
  x := 2
}|||{
  r1 := x
}
%% allow ((2,3) ∈ .co) []
